WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:05.780
Apple is diving head-first into the streaming
wars, with a new slate of original programming.

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:08.160
That sounds great, but what does it all mean?

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:12.120
From the shows you'll get to the price you'll
pay for it, we've rounded up everything you

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:14.240
need to know about Apple TV+.

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:16.700
"Let's talk about Apple TV+."

00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:22.640
Everyone clutching their wallets can breathe
a sigh of relief.

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:28.140
Apple TV+ is going to be among the most affordable
of the major streaming services, launching

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:30.000
at only $4.99 per month.

00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:35.800
This is less than half the cost of Netflix's
most popular plan, which is $12.99 per month,

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:38.560
or Hulu's ad-free plan at $11.99.

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:43.180
It's also less than a third of the cost of
the upcoming HBO Max, which is likely to cost

00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:45.920
anywhere from $15 to $18 per month.

00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:51.720
More comparable to the price point of Apple
TV+ are CBS All Access at $5.99 per month,

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:57.660
Hulu's $5.99 ad-supported plan, and Disney+,
which will cost $6.99 per month when it launches

00:00:57.660 --> 00:00:58.400
in November.

00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:03.059
However, for early birds who jumped on Disney's
special offer and paid up-front in August

00:01:03.059 --> 00:01:08.210
of 2019, they'll have gotten the best bargain
of all, snagging Disney+ for three years for

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:09.900
less than $4 per month.

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:12.380
It's a commitment, but a cheap commitment.

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:17.520
Right now, Apple TV+ can't compete with that
not unless they also decide to roll out a

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:21.900
similar discount, designed to tie subscribers
to their service for a few years.

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:27.000
Just a little over seven months after the
tech company first announced their new streaming

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:31.280
service, Apple TV+ will hit screens beginning
on November 1, 2019.

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:35.960
The app will launch simultaneously in over
100 countries and regions, meaning that no

00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:40.130
matter where you're located, there's a pretty
good chance you'll be able to access the service

00:01:40.130 --> 00:01:41.440
before the end of the year.

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:46.280
This is a significantly larger reach than
Disney+, which launches two weeks later in

00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:47.640
only three countries.

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:51.740
Disney has said they expect their streaming
service to be available in all major markets

00:01:51.740 --> 00:01:56.500
within two years, which means it will likely
take them a while to catch up to Apple's substantial

00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:57.000
lead.

00:01:57.240 --> 00:02:02.060
However, the scope of both services pales
in comparison to Netflix, which is already

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:07.600
available in more than 190 countries, and
is probably their most formidable competition.

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:12.780
Unlike other streaming services such as Netflix,
Hulu, and Disney+, which stream their own

00:02:12.790 --> 00:02:17.930
original movies and TV series alongside an
expansive catalog of licensed and archival

00:02:17.930 --> 00:02:22.640
content, Apple TV+ intends to launch with
an all-original slate of movies and shows.

00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:27.980
Apple has reportedly spent upwards of $6 billion
on their original content, which includes

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:31.200
a number of new shows starring some of the
biggest names in Hollywood.

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:35.840
So far, we know of nine confirmed titles that
will be available upon the service's launch

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:39.340
on November 1, 2019, although more are likely
on the way.

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:44.599
These include The Morning Show, a behind the
scenes TV drama starring Jennifer Aniston,

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:46.390
Reese Witherspoon, and Steve Carell;

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:49.920
See, a speculative sci-fi series starring
Jason Momoa;

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:55.020
and Dickinson, a comedic take on the life
of poet Emily Dickinson starring Hailee Steinfeld.

00:02:55.260 --> 00:03:00.440
Also at launch, Apple TV+ will boast the new
series Ghostwriter, Helpsters, For All Mankind,

00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:05.100
and an original show from Oprah focusing on
the topic of mental health.

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:09.739
Dozens of other shows are also in various
stages of production, with release dates still

00:03:09.740 --> 00:03:10.740
to be announced.

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:11.940
"We'll go to Mars.

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:13.200
Saturn.

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:14.200
Stars.

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:15.360
The galaxy."

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:20.180
While Apple TV+ will be launching with a number
of original series and the company has said

00:03:20.180 --> 00:03:24.860
that feature films will be a significant part
of its offering going forward, only two feature-length

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:27.360
originals have been announced to be available
at launch.

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:32.231
One is the documentary The Elephant Queen,
which is narrated by Chiwetel Ejiofor and

00:03:32.231 --> 00:03:36.269
follows a mother elephant and her herd on
their search for a new watering hole.

00:03:36.269 --> 00:03:41.209
The other is Snoopy in Space, an animated
film focusing on the Peanuts characters.

00:03:41.209 --> 00:03:45.849
Otherwise, Apple has announced only one feature
film in the works: On the Rocks, starring

00:03:45.849 --> 00:03:50.200
Bill Murray and Rashida Jones and directed
by Sofia Coppola, which will follow a young

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:52.940
mother as she attempts to reconnect to her
wealthy father.

00:03:53.160 --> 00:03:57.439
Despite the slim pickings at launch, Apple
does intend to build a robust slate of original

00:03:57.440 --> 00:04:00.120
films to stream alongside its original series.

00:04:00.430 --> 00:04:05.640
In November of 2018, the company announced
its partnership with film studio A24, which

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:08.720
will produce multiple films that will play
on Apple TV+.

00:04:08.909 --> 00:04:15.159
A24's past films include numerous Oscar winners
and nominees, including Lady Bird, Ex Machina,

00:04:15.160 --> 00:04:15.660
and Moonlight.

00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:19.830
Their deal with Apple seems to indicate that
not only will the tech giant be taking its

00:04:19.830 --> 00:04:23.960
film slate seriously, but that it'll also
be angling for some major awards.

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:29.260
Although Apple TV+'s five-dollar price point
is about as affordable as streaming service

00:04:29.261 --> 00:04:34.070
subscriptions come, there's a way to get your
subscription for even less money month-to-month,

00:04:34.070 --> 00:04:36.880
although it requires a hefty up-front cost.

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:42.480
Starting on September 10, 2019, Apple began
including a free year-long subscription to

00:04:42.480 --> 00:04:48.640
Apple TV+ with the purchase of any new or
refurbished iPhone, iPad, Apple TV, iPod touch,

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:49.240
or Mac.

00:04:49.420 --> 00:04:53.700
Plus, through the use of Family Sharing, up
to five more of your family members can also

00:04:53.700 --> 00:04:56.160
access the service using your free subscription.

00:04:56.490 --> 00:04:59.860
However, "free" in this case is only from
a certain point of view.

00:04:59.870 --> 00:05:03.920
While it's true that your bank account won't
be charged the $4.99 per month fee for Apple

00:05:03.920 --> 00:05:08.300
TV+ if you purchase a new Apple device, you're
still out the cost of the device.

00:05:08.790 --> 00:05:13.440
So as tempting as the idea of a "free" year-long
subscription might seem, it's probably only

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:17.240
a good deal if you were already in the market
for a new Apple device anyway.

00:05:17.780 --> 00:05:22.880
Once Apple TV+ launches, there will be a number
of convenient ways for you to access the service

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:25.920
assuming, that is, you're already an Apple
customer.

00:05:26.050 --> 00:05:31.120
The Apple TV app comes pre-installed on iPhone,
iPad, Apple TV, and iPod touch.

00:05:31.120 --> 00:05:35.830
In order to play Apple TV+ content, your device
will likely need to be running a recent version

00:05:35.830 --> 00:05:42.050
of Apple's software, meaning you'll need to
have updated to iOS 12.3 or later, tvOS 12.3

00:05:42.050 --> 00:05:44.300
or later, or macOS Catalina.

00:05:44.520 --> 00:05:49.230
You'll also be able to access the Apple TV
app through some Samsung smart TVs, and in

00:05:49.230 --> 00:05:55.120
the future, you can expect to see the app
show up on Amazon Fire TV, LG, Roku, Sony,

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:56.430
and VIZIO platforms.

00:05:56.430 --> 00:06:01.140
However, if you don't own an Apple device
or a supported Samsung TV, and if you're not

00:06:01.140 --> 00:06:05.130
in the market to upgrade your devices to a
supported model in the near future, your only

00:06:05.130 --> 00:06:10.410
option for watching Apple TV+ content will
be through your web browser at tv.apple.com,

00:06:10.410 --> 00:06:13.280
where you can sign up for the service and
stream content.

00:06:13.500 --> 00:06:18.620
Unlike Disney+, which supports a wider variety
of devices, Apple has announced no plans to

00:06:18.620 --> 00:06:23.220
make their app available on Chromecast, PlayStation,
Xbox, or Android devices.

00:06:23.780 --> 00:06:25.380
"What happened to your TV?"

00:06:26.280 --> 00:06:27.420
"We had a disagreement."

00:06:27.600 --> 00:06:32.020
Although most of the shows and movies currently
announced for Apple TV+ will be in English,

00:06:32.030 --> 00:06:35.880
the service will have a number of options
available to make its content more accessible

00:06:35.880 --> 00:06:39.380
for subscribers who speak other languages
or are hard of hearing.

00:06:39.520 --> 00:06:44.840
At launch, Apple TV+ content will be subtitled
or dubbed in nearly 40 different languages,

00:06:44.840 --> 00:06:48.620
including Subtitles for the Deaf and Hard-of-Hearing
and closed captions.

00:06:48.900 --> 00:06:53.340
Additionally, all of the content available
on Apple TV+ will be available with audio

00:06:53.350 --> 00:06:55.500
descriptions in eight languages.

00:06:55.500 --> 00:07:00.211
In order to activate a show or film's accessibility
features and change your audio options, you'll

00:07:00.211 --> 00:07:04.900
simply go to the title's information page
in the iTunes store or Apple TV app and scroll

00:07:04.900 --> 00:07:09.950
to either the Languages or Accessibility section,
depending on which functionality you need.

00:07:09.950 --> 00:07:14.870
More information on how to enable subtitles
or audio descriptions in your Apple TV app

00:07:14.870 --> 00:07:16.600
is available on Apple's website.

00:07:17.240 --> 00:07:21.900
Oftentimes, it can be convenient to be able
to download a show or film from a streaming

00:07:21.900 --> 00:07:22.980
service to watch offline.

00:07:23.180 --> 00:07:27.640
Maybe you're traveling or heading to a place
with limited internet access, or maybe your

00:07:27.640 --> 00:07:31.680
internet connection is glitchy and you want
to ensure you'll be able to watch your selection

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:34.240
without worrying that it will start freezing
or skipping.

00:07:34.420 --> 00:07:39.120
Fortunately, Apple has confirmed that Apple
TV+ will include a download option for its

00:07:39.130 --> 00:07:43.430
original content, giving you the freedom to
save a title to your device to watch at your

00:07:43.430 --> 00:07:45.220
convenience, no matter where you are.

00:07:45.560 --> 00:07:50.560
What's less clear is exactly what sorts of
restrictions Apple will be placing on downloads.

00:07:50.560 --> 00:07:54.500
It's likely that the service may place limits
on how many shows you can download at one

00:07:54.500 --> 00:07:57.380
time, or on how many times you can download
the same show.

00:07:57.440 --> 00:08:01.820
It also may restrict your ability to download
the same show or film on multiple devices

00:08:01.830 --> 00:08:06.400
at once, and download options may vary depending
on your subscription option and what sort

00:08:06.400 --> 00:08:07.700
of device you're using.

00:08:08.320 --> 00:08:12.680
It's almost hard to remember a time when streaming
services didn't grant us access to entire

00:08:12.680 --> 00:08:15.080
seasons of television series all at once.

00:08:15.220 --> 00:08:19.880
Netflix popularized the full-season binge
model, which is also how Amazon Prime releases

00:08:19.880 --> 00:08:20.780
their series.

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:25.600
Other services such as Hulu and the upcoming
Disney+, though, go against that trend by

00:08:25.600 --> 00:08:28.490
sticking to a one-new-episode-per-week schedule.

00:08:28.490 --> 00:08:32.810
Now, every time a new streaming service is
announced, one of the first questions potential

00:08:32.810 --> 00:08:37.261
subscribers ask is whether its shows will
be released all at once, or one episode at

00:08:37.261 --> 00:08:37.780
a time.

00:08:38.120 --> 00:08:42.860
Apple TV+ will actually be taking a bit of
a hybrid approach to their release schedule,

00:08:42.860 --> 00:08:47.360
marrying binge and weekly release models together
for a format that allows viewers to binge

00:08:47.360 --> 00:08:52.160
just enough to get hooked on a series, but
then requires them to exercise patience for

00:08:52.160 --> 00:08:52.740
the rest.

00:08:53.160 --> 00:08:58.040
While some series will have their full seasons
become available all at once, most Apple TV+

00:08:58.040 --> 00:09:02.200
shows will premiere with three episodes, and
then move to a one-a-week schedule.

00:09:02.370 --> 00:09:06.560
So if you want to binge an entire season of
an Apple TV+ show in one sitting, you're out

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:10.140
of luck unless you're willing to wait until
after the full season has aired.

00:09:10.900 --> 00:09:16.260
Unlike other streaming services such as Netflix,
Hulu, Amazon Prime, and CBS All Access, or

00:09:16.261 --> 00:09:21.960
upcoming services such as Disney+ and HBO
Max, Apple TV+ is unique in its approach to

00:09:21.960 --> 00:09:26.300
its streaming library, in that it won't include
any licensed content at all.

00:09:26.300 --> 00:09:30.470
Basically, what this means is that you shouldn't
expect to see any old favorites show up on

00:09:30.470 --> 00:09:31.280
Apple TV+.

00:09:31.660 --> 00:09:35.720
Their entire streaming library will be made
up of originals that haven't ever previously

00:09:35.720 --> 00:09:40.360
aired anywhere else, and which you won't be
able to find on any other streaming service.

00:09:40.480 --> 00:09:45.800
Everything you watch on Apple TV+ can only
be watched on Apple TV+, and won't include

00:09:45.800 --> 00:09:47.380
anything you've ever seen before.

00:09:47.660 --> 00:09:53.040
This explains Apple's staggering $6 billion
investment in original content for Apple TV+.

00:09:53.460 --> 00:09:57.830
Since it will be the only streaming service
with an entirely original slate of shows and

00:09:57.830 --> 00:10:01.550
films, it makes sense that the company is
sinking a significant amount of money into

00:10:01.550 --> 00:10:06.070
making sure they produce a wide variety of
high quality content that will keep viewers

00:10:06.070 --> 00:10:06.740
engaged.

00:10:07.070 --> 00:10:11.080
However, it's worth noting that Apple's budget
still doesn't come close to the money Netflix

00:10:11.080 --> 00:10:16.500
spends on original content, which is expected
to hit $15 billion by the end of 2019.

00:10:17.140 --> 00:10:22.260
For individuals curious about Apple TV+ who
don't necessarily want to commit to the $4.99

00:10:22.260 --> 00:10:26.370
per month subscription cost, and don't want
to purchase a new device in order to receive

00:10:26.370 --> 00:10:28.880
a free subscription, you're still kind of
in luck.

00:10:29.120 --> 00:10:34.031
Apple TV+ will be offering a free seven-day
trial for customers new to the service, starting

00:10:34.040 --> 00:10:35.440
at launch on November 1.

00:10:35.830 --> 00:10:40.100
The free trial will give subscribers access
to all of the service's features, and will

00:10:40.100 --> 00:10:43.520
be available across all of their devices,
just like the paid service.

00:10:43.970 --> 00:10:48.200
At the end of the seven days, your Apple TV+
subscription will automatically renew at the

00:10:48.200 --> 00:10:53.160
$4.99 per month rate, which will then continue
to renew monthly until you cancel the service.

00:10:53.440 --> 00:10:57.200
In order to avoid being charged after your
trial, you'll need to make sure to cancel

00:10:57.200 --> 00:11:01.470
the subscription before your seven days are
complete but of course, by then, Apple is

00:11:01.470 --> 00:11:05.580
hoping you'll be hooked on the streaming service,
and will gladly shell out your hard-earned

00:11:05.580 --> 00:11:08.480
five dollars per month in order to keep watching.

